WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:08.140
A job search is a hundred open loops. Dozens of roles, hundreds of emails, interviews and follow-ups — and all of it living in your head.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.750
This is CareerOps. Your job search, continuously understood.

3
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:19.930
It plugs into the tools you already live in — your Gmail, your calendar, your meeting notes in Granola — and reads them, so you don't have to.

4
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.640
Every morning, it tells you what to do first, and why. What's overdue, what's waiting, what deserves attention.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.880
Your inbox files itself. Every message matched to the right role, with a reply already written.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.900
Nothing gets lost. Every posting, every email, every conversation — kept, even after the listing comes down.

7
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.210
And it finds what you couldn't: the one question you keep getting wrong, and what to fix before the next round.

8
00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.240
Underneath, a team of specialist agents works your search — reading, matching, drafting, and prioritising every move.

9
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.750
It drafts, it ranks, it recommends. But it never sends. You decide.

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.110
CareerOps. Your job search, continuously understood.
